WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:03.270
We often treat public health funding as overhead.

2
00:00:03.594 --> 00:00:05.286
A budget line item to trim.

3
00:00:05.898 --> 00:00:10.662
But treating healthcare as a residual cost quietly breaks the broader economy.

4
00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:16.774
Take a rural Michigan hospital facing sudden revenue gaps after pandemic Medicaid funding expired.

5
00:00:17.418 --> 00:00:19.686
To survive the year, the clinic reacts.

6
00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:24.038
They freeze hiring, stall capital projects, and trim prevention programs.

7
00:00:24.586 --> 00:00:26.598
But hospitals don't close overnight.

8
00:00:27.082 --> 00:00:30.918
The structural damage accumulates quietly as deferred maintenance.

9
00:00:31.274 --> 00:00:35.014
Creating a false illusion of stability for the short-term budget cycle.

10
00:00:35.722 --> 00:00:37.030
When prevention is weakened,

11
00:00:37.322 --> 00:00:38.758
costs don't disappear.

12
00:00:39.082 --> 00:00:40.070
They surface later

13
00:00:40.362 --> 00:00:45.318
as a surge of high-cost emergency cases that overwhelm the fragile system.

14
00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:48.678
Because healthcare is a load-bearing economic pillar,

15
00:00:48.906 --> 00:00:50.790
Its failure doesn't stay isolated.

16
00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.094
It hollows out local employment.

17
00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:56.870
Drives up disability rates, and drains workforce productivity.

18
00:00:57.546 --> 00:00:59.782
But with predictable long-term investment.

19
00:01:00.042 --> 00:01:02.598
The health system becomes a generational asset.

20
00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:07.206
Capable of absorbing economic shocks rather than transferring them to the community.

21
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:08.966
And that rural hospital,

22
00:01:09.418 --> 00:01:14.470
When funded as foundational economic infrastructure, it doesn't just survive the budget year.

23
00:01:14.954 --> 00:01:17.702
It actively protects the entire local economy.

24
00:01:18.314 --> 00:01:19.590
Human in purpose.

25
00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.062
Systemic in method.

26
00:01:21.482 --> 00:01:22.790
Protective in outcome.
